{"excerpt_id":"ex_cef2c31af42d_012","source_id":"src_cef2c31af42d","source_hash":"56cc0d3331a4c888e4cfc62c58fbe53201fe0d122d57cbb52b27a0aa14c54662","text":"Copy page as Markdown for LLMs","location_hint":"paragraph 81","char_start":1760,"char_end":1790,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:50:50.039Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_cef2c31af42d_013","source_id":"src_cef2c31af42d","source_hash":"56cc0d3331a4c888e4cfc62c58fbe53201fe0d122d57cbb52b27a0aa14c54662","text":"An \"Account\" in the XRP Ledger represents a holder of XRP and a sender of transactions .","location_hint":"paragraph 92","char_start":2048,"char_end":2136,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:50:50.039Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_cef2c31af42d_014","source_id":"src_cef2c31af42d","source_hash":"56cc0d3331a4c888e4cfc62c58fbe53201fe0d122d57cbb52b27a0aa14c54662","text":"An account consists of an address, an XRP balance, a sequence number, and a history of its transactions. To be able to send transactions, the owner also needs one or more cryptographic key pairs associated with the account.","location_hint":"paragraph 93","char_start":2138,"char_end":2361,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:50:50.039Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_cef2c31af42d_015","source_id":"src_cef2c31af42d","source_hash":"56cc0d3331a4c888e4cfc62c58fbe53201fe0d122d57cbb52b27a0aa14c54662","text":"The core elements of an account are:","location_hint":"paragraph 95","char_start":2382,"char_end":2418,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:50:50.039Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_cef2c31af42d_016","source_id":"src_cef2c31af42d","source_hash":"56cc0d3331a4c888e4cfc62c58fbe53201fe0d122d57cbb52b27a0aa14c54662","text":"An identifying address , such as rf1BiGeXwwQoi8Z2ueFYTEXSwuJYfV2Jpn .","location_hint":"paragraph 96","char_start":2422,"char_end":2491,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:50:50.039Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_cef2c31af42d_017","source_id":"src_cef2c31af42d","source_hash":"56cc0d3331a4c888e4cfc62c58fbe53201fe0d122d57cbb52b27a0aa14c54662","text":"An XRP balance . Some of this XRP is set aside for the Reserve .","location_hint":"paragraph 97","char_start":2493,"char_end":2557,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:50:50.039Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_cef2c31af42d_018","source_id":"src_cef2c31af42d","source_hash":"56cc0d3331a4c888e4cfc62c58fbe53201fe0d122d57cbb52b27a0aa14c54662","text":"A sequence number , which helps make sure any transactions this account sends are applied in the correct order and only once. To execute a transaction, the transaction&#x27;s sequence number and its sender&#x27;s sequence number must match. Then, as part of applying the transaction, the account&#x27;s sequence number increases by 1. (See also: Basic Data Types: Account Sequence .)","location_hint":"paragraph 98","char_start":2559,"char_end":2942,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:50:50.039Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_cef2c31af42d_019","source_id":"src_cef2c31af42d","source_hash":"56cc0d3331a4c888e4cfc62c58fbe53201fe0d122d57cbb52b27a0aa14c54662","text":"A history of transactions that affected this account and its balances.","location_hint":"paragraph 99","char_start":2944,"char_end":3014,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:50:50.039Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_cef2c31af42d_020","source_id":"src_cef2c31af42d","source_hash":"56cc0d3331a4c888e4cfc62c58fbe53201fe0d122d57cbb52b27a0aa14c54662","text":"One or more ways to authorize transactions , possibly including:","location_hint":"paragraph 100","char_start":3016,"char_end":3080,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:50:50.039Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_cef2c31af42d_021","source_id":"src_cef2c31af42d","source_hash":"56cc0d3331a4c888e4cfc62c58fbe53201fe0d122d57cbb52b27a0aa14c54662","text":"A master key pair intrinsic to the account. (This can be disabled but not changed.)","location_hint":"paragraph 101","char_start":3082,"char_end":3165,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:50:50.039Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_cef2c31af42d_022","source_id":"src_cef2c31af42d","source_hash":"56cc0d3331a4c888e4cfc62c58fbe53201fe0d122d57cbb52b27a0aa14c54662","text":"A \"regular\" key pair that can be rotated.","location_hint":"paragraph 102","char_start":3167,"char_end":3208,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:50:50.039Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_cef2c31af42d_023","source_id":"src_cef2c31af42d","source_hash":"56cc0d3331a4c888e4cfc62c58fbe53201fe0d122d57cbb52b27a0aa14c54662","text":"A signer list for multi-signing . (Stored separately from the account&#x27;s core data.)","location_hint":"paragraph 103","char_start":3210,"char_end":3298,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:50:50.039Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_cef2c31af42d_024","source_id":"src_cef2c31af42d","source_hash":"56cc0d3331a4c888e4cfc62c58fbe53201fe0d122d57cbb52b27a0aa14c54662","text":"An account&#x27;s core data is stored in an AccountRoot ledger entry. An account can also be the owner (or partial owner) of several other types of ledger entry.","location_hint":"paragraph 104","char_start":3304,"char_end":3465,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:50:50.039Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_cef2c31af42d_025","source_id":"src_cef2c31af42d","source_hash":"56cc0d3331a4c888e4cfc62c58fbe53201fe0d122d57cbb52b27a0aa14c54662","text":"An \"Account\" in the XRP Ledger is somewhere between the financial usage (like \"bank account\") and the computing usage (like \"UNIX account\"). Non-XRP currencies and assets aren&#x27;t stored in an XRP Ledger Account itself; each such asset is stored in an accounting relationship called a \"Trust Line\" that connects two parties.","location_hint":"paragraph 106","char_start":3474,"char_end":3801,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:50:50.039Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_cef2c31af42d_026","source_id":"src_cef2c31af42d","source_hash":"56cc0d3331a4c888e4cfc62c58fbe53201fe0d122d57cbb52b27a0aa14c54662","text":"There is not a dedicated \"create account\" transaction. The Payment transaction automatically creates a new account if the payment sends enough XRP to a mathematically-valid address that does not already have an account. This is called funding an account, and creates an AccountRoot entry in the ledger. No other transaction can create an account.","location_hint":"paragraph 108","char_start":3822,"char_end":4168,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:50:50.039Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_cef2c31af42d_027","source_id":"src_cef2c31af42d","source_hash":"56cc0d3331a4c888e4cfc62c58fbe53201fe0d122d57cbb52b27a0aa14c54662","text":"Funding an account does not give you any special privileges over that account. Whoever has the secret key corresponding to the account&#x27;s address has full control over the account and all XRP it contains. For some addresses, it&#x27;s possible that no one has the secret key, in which case the account is a black hole and the XRP is lost forever.","location_hint":"paragraph 110","char_start":4181,"char_end":4531,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:50:50.039Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_cef2c31af42d_028","source_id":"src_cef2c31af42d","source_hash":"56cc0d3331a4c888e4cfc62c58fbe53201fe0d122d57cbb52b27a0aa14c54662","text":"The typical way to get an account in the XRP Ledger is as follows:","location_hint":"paragraph 111","char_start":4533,"char_end":4599,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:50:50.039Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_cef2c31af42d_029","source_id":"src_cef2c31af42d","source_hash":"56cc0d3331a4c888e4cfc62c58fbe53201fe0d122d57cbb52b27a0aa14c54662","text":"Generate a key pair from a strong source of randomness and calculate the address of that key pair.","location_hint":"paragraph 112","char_start":4603,"char_end":4701,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:50:50.039Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_cef2c31af42d_030","source_id":"src_cef2c31af42d","source_hash":"56cc0d3331a4c888e4cfc62c58fbe53201fe0d122d57cbb52b27a0aa14c54662","text":"Have someone who already has an account in the XRP Ledger send XRP to the address you generated.","location_hint":"paragraph 113","char_start":4703,"char_end":4799,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:50:50.039Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_cef2c31af42d_031","source_id":"src_cef2c31af42d","source_hash":"56cc0d3331a4c888e4cfc62c58fbe53201fe0d122d57cbb52b27a0aa14c54662","text":"For example, you can buy XRP in a private exchange, then withdraw XRP from the exchange to the address you specified.","location_hint":"paragraph 114","char_start":4803,"char_end":4920,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:50:50.039Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_cef2c31af42d_032","source_id":"src_cef2c31af42d","source_hash":"56cc0d3331a4c888e4cfc62c58fbe53201fe0d122d57cbb52b27a0aa14c54662","text":"The first time you receive XRP at your own XRP Ledger address, you must pay the account reserve (currently 1 XRP ), which locks up that amount of XRP indefinitely. In contrast, private exchanges usually hold all their customers&#x27; XRP in a few shared XRP Ledger accounts, so customers don&#x27;t have to pay the reserve for individual accounts at the exchange. Before withdrawing, consider whether having your own account directly on the XRP Ledger is worth the price.","location_hint":"paragraph 116","char_start":4933,"char_end":5404,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:50:50.039Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_cef2c31af42d_033","source_id":"src_cef2c31af42d","source_hash":"56cc0d3331a4c888e4cfc62c58fbe53201fe0d122d57cbb52b27a0aa14c54662","text":"Issuing and Operational Addresses","location_hint":"paragraph 121","char_start":5463,"char_end":5496,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T18:50:50.039Z"}
